          <li><b>Film</b><span>Dialogue on the screen, music around you, effects where they happen</span></li>
        </ul>
        <div class="sp-auto-grid">
          <div>
            <b>It listens first</b>
            <p>Sound recognition on the Neural Engine hears what is playing: which instruments, which voices, music or speech, and how big the room was. That decides the venue, and it tells you why. Never Private Cloud Compute.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <b>Every instrument, every frequency</b>
            <p>Each instrument and voice becomes its own object you can move, like the spacetime bubble above. Bass stays close and centred, and the air above 6 kHz opens up and rises, the way your ears expect.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <b>Nothing added, nothing lost</b>
            <p>The goal: the parts add back up to the original, so folding it to stereo gives you the artist’s master. Today’s split doesn’t reach that yet, so one tap always plays the original itself, and artists can switch nu.eq off for their work.</p>
